@startuml
title SFT composition pipeline — T₁ ∘ T₂ (the output algebra of T₁ is the input algebra of T₂)

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.3
skinparam sequence {
  ParticipantBorderColor #1F2937
  ParticipantFontColor #111827
  LifeLineBorderColor #9CA3AF
  ArrowFontColor #111827
}

participant "Input\n(A*)" as IN #DBEAFE
participant "T₁ : A → B*" as T1 #EDE9FE
participant "T₂ : B → C*" as T2 #EDE9FE
participant "Output\n(C*)" as OUT #FCE7F3

IN -> T1 : word over A
activate T1
T1 -> T2 : intermediate B*
activate T2
T2 -> OUT : C*
deactivate T2
deactivate T1

note over T1, T2
  compose::<C> builds the product T₁ ∘ T₂ — ONE transducer,
  not a runtime chain. The middle algebra B must match
  (output of T₁ = input of T₂), which is exactly why
  composability requires the middle algebra to agree.
  Composition preserves functionality
  (compose_preserves_functional, SftFunctionality.v):
  chaining single-valued transducers stays single-valued.
end note

legend bottom
|= Color |= Stage |
|<#DBEAFE> | input word over algebra A |
|<#EDE9FE> | symbolic transducer stage (SFT) |
|<#FCE7F3> | emitted output word over algebra C |
endlegend
@enduml
